<section class="section" aria-labelledby="why-title">
  <div class="container split">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Why InspectX</p>
      <h2 id="why-title">Inspections that are faster, traceable and ready for audit</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Compliance is critical in hazardous areas. Periodic inspection of hazardous area equipment is governed by SANS 60079-17, which sets out the requirements for visual, close and detailed inspections of installed equipment. The interval between periodic inspections shall not exceed three years without seeking expert advice.</p>
        <p>Paper-based inspections make that difficult to manage: records are hard to find, equipment histories are scattered and defects can go unresolved. InspectX turns the process into a streamlined, digital-first system designed for accuracy, accountability and ease of use.</p>
        <p>With QR-code-enabled inspections, users can instantly retrieve equipment histories and conduct thorough assessments. Automated data logging and cloud storage ensure every inspection is securely recorded, providing a clear audit trail.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <blockquote class="quote-block">
        <p>“Lose the paperwork and switch to a fast, QR-code-driven digital inspection system.”</p>
        <cite>InspectX</cite>
      </blockquote>
      <h3 class="group-label mt-2">Inspection disciplines</h3>
      <ul class="disciplines">
        <li>{% icon "shield-check" %}<span>HazLoc <small>Hazardous locations (Ex)</small></span></li>
        <li>{% icon "zap" %}<span>Earthing</span></li>
        <li>{% icon "cable" %}<span>Electrical &amp; Instrumentation</span></li>
        <li>{% icon "layers" %}<span>MCCs &amp; DB boards</span></li>
        <li>{% icon "wrench" %}<span>Mechanical</span></li>
        <li>{% icon "building-2" %}<span>Maintenance <small>Conveyors, cooling towers, boiler houses, structures</small></span></li>
        <li>{% icon "scan-line" %}<span>Access control for vehicles</span></li>
        <li>{% icon "calendar-clock" %}<span>Daily, weekly, monthly or periodic <small>Visual, close and detailed</small></span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
